      "id": "d70514339ef3-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "A light bulb working on a 18 V battery draws a current of 3 A. What will be the resistance of the bulb? 18 V &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2376;&#2335;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358; &#2348;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 3 A &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2343; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A light bulb working on a 18 V battery draws a current of 3 A. What will be the resistance of the bulb?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>18 V &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2376;&#2335;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358; &#2348;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 3 A &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2343; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "6 &#937; 6 &#937;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">6 &#937;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 &#937;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "2 &#937; 2 &#937;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">2 &#937;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2 &#937;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4 &#937; 4 &#937;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">4 &#937;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#937;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "3 &#937; 3 &#937;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">3 &#937;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 &#937;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>The measure of opposition applied by any object to the flow of electric current is known as resistance.</p><p>Resistance Formula is R = V/I.</p><p>Here, V = 18 Volt and I = 3A</p><p>R= 18/3 = 6 &#937;</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d70514339ef3-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Identify the formula that represents Ohm's law. &#2323;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2361;&#2330;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Identify the formula that represents Ohm's law.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2323;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2361;&#2330;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "V = A +&#937;&#8239; V = A +&#937;&#8239;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">V = A +&#937;&#8239;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">V = A +&#937;&#8239;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "A = V x &#937; A = V x &#937;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">A = V x &#937;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A = V x &#937;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "&#937;&#8239; = A x V &#937;&#8239; = A x V",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">&#937;&#8239; = A x V</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#937;&#8239; = A x V</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "V = A x &#937;&#8239; V = A x &#937;&#8239;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">V = A x &#937;&#8239;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">V = A x &#937;&#8239;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Ohm's law states the relationship between current (A), voltage (V), and resistance (&#937;&#8239;). The amount of steady current through a large number of materials is directly proportional to the potential difference, or voltage, across the materials. <b>The formula that represents - V = A x &#937;&#8239;.</b></p>",
