    {
      "id": "d70514339ef3-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "Which of the following is NOT a conductor? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2369;&#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is NOT a conductor?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2369;&#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325; <b>&#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;</b> &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Hard rubber &#2325;&#2336;&#2379;&#2352; &#2352;&#2348;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Hard rubber</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2336;&#2379;&#2352; &#2352;&#2348;&#2352;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Copper &#2340;&#2366;&#2305;&#2348;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Copper</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2305;&#2348;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Silver &#2330;&#2366;&#2305;&#2342;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Silver</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2366;&#2305;&#2342;&#2368;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Nickel &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Nickel</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p><b>Hard rubber</b> is not a conductor of electricity because it is an insulator. Insulators, like hard rubber, have high resistance to the flow of electric current. They do not allow electric charges to move freely through them and therefore do not conduct electricity.</p>",
